   "source": [
    "Note how $V_{2}$ (the output taken from across $C_{1}$) has decreased from the input magnitude of 1 to about 0.7, and the magnitude at $V_{filt}$ is significantly lower. If you were to plot the voltage across all the capacitors, you would see a steady decrease. However, at $V_{out}$, we can select a gain to boost the signal. You may find it helpful to remember that the formula for the gain of a non-inverting op-amp is $1+\\frac{R_2}{R_1}$. I used $R_1$ as 1k$\\ohm$ because it's simpler. Since I want the output's peak amplitude to be the same as the input, we can just divide 1 by the amplitude at the end of the lowpass filter. As seen in Figure 5, I would need a gain of ~7.25, hence $R_2$ being 6.2k$\\ohm$.\n",
    "\n"
