   "source": [
    "# Conclusion\n",
    "In this Notebook, we've looked into FFTs and two different types of lowpass filter implementations in both their digital and analogue representations. We've seen that while a Butterworth filter is more complex in design and often requires a higher order, it preserves the original audio (without the noise, of course) the best. This is because of its maximally flat passband and sharper roll-off. Alternative designs like a Chebyshev filter offer an even steeper roll-off, but no maximally flat passband."
   ]
